# Written by Infrar, inside the directory Infrar owns. Nothing outside it is touched,
# and this file changes how git merges ONLY the files it names.
#
# -merge: do not line-merge a generated file. On a conflict git then writes no conflict
# markers and leaves one whole, valid side in the tree — instead of interleaving two
# generated files into text that describes neither branch, and that for a manifest is not
# even parseable. The path is still recorded as conflicted: nothing is decided for you.
# The answer to a conflict here is to regenerate the file, which Infrar does when it is
# the one merging; anywhere else, take either side and let the next analysis rewrite it.
#
# linguist-generated / gitlab-generated: ask the code host to collapse these in a
# pull-request diff. Hosts that do not know them ignore them.
#
# Everything NOT listed below merges normally, on purpose — build.yaml is authored and two
# branches adding different env entries must genuinely combine, and lessons.md is appended
# memory that is never regenerated.

.gitattributes  -merge linguist-generated=true gitlab-generated
root.md         -merge linguist-generated=true gitlab-generated
knowledge.md    -merge linguist-generated=true gitlab-generated
commit.md       -merge linguist-generated=true gitlab-generated
iac-preview/**  -merge linguist-generated=true gitlab-generated
